  "notation": "En 1018.05",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html",
  "prefLabel": "En 1018.05 Insurance Thresholds",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1018.05 Insurance Thresholds. A utility shall require an applicant to purchase insurance covering utility damages as follows:\n\n(a) For non-inverter-based facilities, the following:\n\nInsurance Thresholds For Non-Inverter-Based Facilities\n\nNameplate Rating > 5 MW | $5,000,000\n\n1 MW < Nameplate Rating < 5 MW | $2,000,000\n\n100 kW < Nameplate Rating < 1 MW | $1,000,000\n\n10 kW < Nameplate Rating < 100 kW | $500,000\n\nNameplate Rating < 10 kW | Typical Homeowners\n\n(b) For inverter-based facilities, the following:\n\nInsurance Thresholds For Inverter-Based Facilities\n\nNameplate Rating > 5 MW | $2,000,000\n\nMW < Nameplate Rating < 5 MW | $1,000,000\n\nNameplate Rating < 1 MW | No insurance\n\nSource. #14657, eff 9-1-26, EXPIRES: 9-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html"
}
